'''2.''' In ''ship-building'', a curve representing a vertical section of the bow-end of a ship.—'''Bowline on a bight''', {{smaller|a bowline-knot made on the bight of a rope.}}—'''On a bowline''', {{smaller|said of a ship when sailing close to the wind.}}
{{smaller block|The Ayacucho went off ''on a bowline'', which brought her to windward of us.
{{right|''R. H. Dana, Jr.'', Before the Mast.}}}}
'''To check the bowline''', {{smaller|to slacken it when the wind becomes more favorable.}}—'''To sharp the main bowline''' {{smaller|or}} '''hale the bowline''', {{smaller|to pull it harder.}}

